Commit:     yeargun <yeargun24+eddocuvm@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Sep 9 01:51:52 2026 +0000

    8.15: the wide single-use collapse, declared per port (-258 on the fleet)

    Terser's collapse_vars accepts a definition whose value reads the name it
    defines, and a name the function assigns more than once. Neither is a hazard
    for that definition: the counts are now taken per definition, and the read may
    be reached over leaves the value cannot write.

    A win on three ports and a loss on three, so it is a config option rather than
    a default -- remarklil -113, mobxlil -106, remark-gfmlil -39. Fleet -2,006
    against the base, 292 of 292 case-lanes pass.

    Also here, off: the function-declaration respelling (fleet +546) and two
    strictly smaller cleanups (fleet +569) whose size is below the plan search's
    sensitivity to any change in the emission.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012nt4Q2F6S8STwas17acEip

